From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Douglas Panhota <douglaspands@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Input: sun4i-lradc-keys - report a key held before the LRADC
 is enabled

The driver enables only the key down and key up interrupts. A key that
is already held when the LRADC starts converting (held at power on, as
the GA36 does with Vol- to open the device tree list of the initramfs)
never makes the key down transition: the hardware raises "already hold"
instead, which the driver leaves off, so the key reads as released
until it is let go and pressed again (GA36 boot 122, boot-dtb-select
task 6.3).

Enable the channel 0 "already hold" interrupt and take it as a press,
with the same voltage lookup as a key down. The cached keycode keeps a
second report away.

diff --git a/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c b/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c
@@ -122,7 +122,11 @@ static irqreturn_t sun4i_lradc_irq(int irq, void *dev_id)
 		lradc->chan0_keycode = 0;
 	}

-	if ((ints & CHAN0_KEYDOWN_IRQ) && lradc->chan0_keycode == 0) {
+	/*
+	 * A key held when the LRADC is enabled (at power on) gives no key down,
+	 * only "already hold": take it as a press too.
+	 */
+	if ((ints & (CHAN0_KEYDOWN_IRQ | CHAN0_ALRDY_HOLD_IRQ)) && lradc->chan0_keycode == 0) {
 		val = readl(lradc->base + LRADC_DATA0) & 0x3f;
 		voltage = val * lradc->vref / 63;

@@ -172,7 +176,8 @@ static int sun4i_lradc_open(struct input_dev *dev)
 	writel(FIRST_CONVERT_DLY(2) | LEVELA_B_CNT(1) | HOLD_EN(1) |
 		SAMPLE_RATE(0) | ENABLE(1), lradc->base + LRADC_CTRL);

-	writel(CHAN0_KEYUP_IRQ | CHAN0_KEYDOWN_IRQ, lradc->base + LRADC_INTC);
+	writel(CHAN0_KEYUP_IRQ | CHAN0_KEYDOWN_IRQ | CHAN0_ALRDY_HOLD_IRQ,
+	       lradc->base + LRADC_INTC);

 	return 0;

